WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
-Our first guest tonight is
a talented singer-songwriter

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.573
and actress who serves as both
an executive producer and star

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.073
of "Only Murders
in the Building,"

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:09.742
which is streaming now on Hulu.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:10.876
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.876 --> 00:00:12.645
-After every date,
I just want to go home

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.781
and plant my face in a pillow
and never go out again.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:18.117
-Okay. Wow.
-Geez.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.619
-You need to relax, okay?

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.921
Just have fun.
Laugh. Flirt.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.923
-Isn't it insulting
to flirt now?

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.591
-Well, who the hell knows?

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.693
Suddenly it's rude to tell
a secretary she looks pretty

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:29.195
in a pair of slacks.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.363
-No.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.364
To that whole sentence.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:33.966
-Compliment her purse.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.168
If it isn't on their body,
you can like it.

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:40.506
-No, again, to every word
that's coming out of your mouth.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:44.010
-Please welcome to the show
and the studio Selena Gomez.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.046
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:49.682
-Hi!

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.183
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:54.019
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:56.522
Thank you.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:57.857
Ah!

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.193
-We're so happy to have you here
with us in New York.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.528
-I'm so happy to be here.
It's my first time.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.864
-It's a lovely, a lovely show,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.066
and it's a really great show
about New York City as well

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.401
that you guys got to shoot here.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.436
-Yeah, I got to live here
for seven months

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.772
and hang out with two legends.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.607
-Really, they are two legends.

00:01:15.607 --> 00:01:16.943
Divas, though, right?

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.411
-Complete divas.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.914
The worst, the most difficult
people I've ever worked with.

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.517
-Yeah, I mean, we were reading
Page Six every day.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.019
Each one wanted a bigger trailer
than the other one.

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.355
-Yeah, it was terrible.
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.857
-And obviously,
you started in TV.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.859
A lot of people know you
from that first.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.860
You haven't done scripted
television in a long time.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.030
Were Steve and Marty
one of the pulls to this

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.533
or did you come to it before
you knew they were involved?

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.535
-No, I always knew
they were involved.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:45.839
But I got a call, and I just --

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.341
I don't know, I love true crime.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.043
And I just -- I have --

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.311
I don't know, the concept
just was so cool,

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:55.214
and I enjoyed working
with both of them.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.682
It's been great.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:59.619
-It is a show about a murder
that takes place in a building,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.889
and three podcast fans
who then both go about

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.391
trying to solve the murder and
starting a podcast themselves.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.159
But you do come by this
honestly.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:09.996
You are being serious when you
say that you like true crime.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.164
-Definitely.
I went to CrimeCon with my mom.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:14.000
-Okay. This is very exciting.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.002
I did not know that
CrimeCon was a thing.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.670
-Nobody does!
I don't know why.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.572
-Well, I mean,
it sounds like a place

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.374
where a crime might be
committed.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.543
You might want to steer clear.
-Yeah, guess so.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.444
I could see that.
-And again, this is no judgment.

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:26.879
I've been to Comic Con
multiple times.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:28.781
Where was the CrimeCon
you went to?

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.783
-We went to Florida.
-Okay.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.919
-And...
-That, by the way, tracks.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:35.255
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.757
-Yes.
Didn't realize that till now.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.092
-Yeah, yeah.
-No, but it's wild.

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.261
They give you a case
that's still open,

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.765
and we are able to solve it
with them.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.599
I mean...
-So, it's not like --

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.401
Okay, so, this is interesting,
because at Comic Con,

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:53.105
it's like, you know, oh, they're
selling comic art over here

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.440
or old back issues there.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.275
This is -- Is it one crime
at CrimeCon?

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.610
-Yeah, basically.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.745
And you're meeting with
the forensic team,

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:01.747
you're meeting with
the family members,

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:03.582
they give you
all the depositions.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.418
I mean, it's completely legit.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.755
I thought I was a full-blown,
like, crime solver.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.924
I felt like I was gonna solve
the case.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.926
-Do you feel like
you were better at it

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:15.294
or your mom was better at it?

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:17.963
-My mom was much better at it
because I was terrible.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.699
-Okay, so, in real life,

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.067
you don't think you could
actually crack a case?

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.568
-Hell no. Nope.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.737
-So, is this --
-Don't come to me.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.739
-So, was this every--
I mean, were you sitting there?

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.407
Were you taking notes?
-Yeah.

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:29.842
-Okay.
-It's just fun.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.578
I don't know how to explain it.
It was a weekend and we...

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:35.248
I don't know, just were around
people that loved it too.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.583
-And then at the end,
is the crime solved?

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.552
-No.
-Okay.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.888
-That's the -- I think
that's the hard part.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:46.359
-Yeah, they say the beginning
of CrimeCon's the most fun.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.027
At the end, they're like,
"Thank you for coming!

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.362
The killer runs free!"
-I know. Exactly.

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:53.832
That's what it felt like.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:55.201
-Did you --
I mean, obviously,

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.869
you're a very
recognizable person.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.238
When you go to CrimeCon, did you
have to go out of your way

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.741
to sort of disguise yourself?
-No, it was great.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.743
People didn't care.
It was so nice.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.178
They were so focused on that.

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.046
And I don't know
if they were my demographic.

00:04:08.046 --> 00:04:10.383
I don't think they gave
a [bleep] that I was there.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.551
-That's true.
Plus, if you wore a disguise,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:14.887
I feel like the one place they
would notice the quickest

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.222
is CrimeCon.
-Yes.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:20.225
-They're very onto things
like disguises.

00:04:20.225 --> 00:04:22.661
You have this situation where
obviously Steve and Marty

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:24.163
have known each other
for a very long time.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.333
I also know them to be
incredibly welcoming people.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.334
It just must have been very fun
to be on set with them.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:30.870
-It really was.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.941
I think they, if anything, have
taught me so much about comedy.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:38.244
I mean, they have a humor that
just doesn't exist anymore.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.246
-Yeah.
-And it's just -- it's the best.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.915
And I love watching them
do what they do.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.417
And I love being a part of it

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:47.553
and trying to live up to it,
you know?

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.422
It's been such a blast.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:52.357
-It's really true what you say.
It doesn't exist anymore.

00:04:52.357 --> 00:04:54.860
But the way they do it
makes it seem very new.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.529
-Yes.
-And I think that speaks to

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.531
how they treat it
so much like a craft.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.865
-Yes. I agree.

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:03.202
And obviously, Steve
I couldn't be more happy for,

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:06.338
'cause this was his baby, too,
with John Hoffman, of course.

00:05:06.338 --> 00:05:07.506
-That's really nice.

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:10.843
So, you have a beauty line.
-Yes.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.845
-And you're also using it
as a platform

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.681
to talk about mental health.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:17.850
Explain why that was important
and how you're marrying the two.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.687
-When I originally wanted
to start a cosmetics line,

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:24.023
I said and I made it very clear

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.859
that I want it to be a brand
that feels effortless,

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:32.031
that feels like it doesn't have
to be about what we look like.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:36.035
So, I just wanted to eliminate
this idea of perfection,

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:38.537
all these girls kind of looking
the same

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.540
and you feel like you need
to look like them.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.643
And I wanted my makeup
to be easy to use

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:49.315
and just something to make women
and men feel comfortable.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.949
I don't know.
It's very important.

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:52.585
-We have some here.
It's called Rare Beauty.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.086
-Yes, it is.

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:57.556
-And this is -- this is what?
What is this?

00:05:57.556 --> 00:05:59.058
-So, this just came out.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.060
This is my mascara.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.763
-Okay, so obviously I've never
applied mascara myself.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:05.264
-And I'm very proud of you.

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:08.434
-We're gonna see exactly
how effortless it is.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.102
-Okay, great.
Let's do it. [ Laughs ]

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.170
-This is so...

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.338
I guess I have, technically.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:14.273
Well, no.
-Have you?

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:15.975
-Well, Rihanna applied it
to me once.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.676
Whatever.
I don't want to talk about it.

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.845
It's something
I'm very private about.

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:21.847
-Oh, my gosh. Okay.

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:25.851
You want to start at the bottom.
-Okay.

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.219
-And then kind of just...

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:29.555
-Well, see, I feel like right
away, it's deeply unfair.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.256
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:33.258
Yeah, go -- then push up.

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:34.760
Oh, wow.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.929
-Right away this is making
a huge difference.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:39.264
-See? [ Laughs ]
-I mean...

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:41.601
-Oh, my gosh, it looks fabulous.
-And also, like --

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.735
You know what?
This is fun to do together.

00:06:43.735 --> 00:06:45.170
-I know. It really is.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.840
-That's the part of this that
I immediately really like.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.709
You know when, like --
I just feel like

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:52.211
there's not a thing guys have
where we're, like,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.713
having a nice conversation,
but also doing something.

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.715
-Yeah, this is very cool.
-This is great.

00:06:56.715 --> 00:07:00.052
I'm just gonna do one eye
so we can see the difference.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.388
-Alright. I just finished both.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.889
-Oh, this is just...
-Alright.

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:05.390
I'm so proud of you.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.027
-I mean, this really
makes a difference.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:09.395
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.464
I mean, I think I -- I thought
this was gonna be like,

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.632
"Ha-ha, you're bad at it
'cause you're a guy,"

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:16.802
but I did great.
-Yeah, you did a great job.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.138
-Now, I do feel like
I got some in my eye.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.472
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.472 --> 00:07:24.810
But can I say, I think it's made
with really good material

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.145
because there's no burning.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.980
-No, that's -- Yes.
-Yeah.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.017
I think I got some in my eye,
and it's just fine.

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:35.354
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:36.855
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:38.157
-Thank you for having me.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.492
-It's really nice to have you
for the first time.

00:07:39.492 --> 00:07:41.560
And again,
the show is wonderful,

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.895
and I can't wait
to watch more of it.

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.396
-Thank you. Appreciate it.

00:07:44.396 --> 00:07:46.064
-You guys, that's Selena Gomez.

00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:48.066
Check out "Only Murders
in the Building" on Hulu now

00:07:48.066 --> 00:07:49.735
with new episodes releasing
on Tuesdays.

